From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-engine <build-engine@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drama3 cuda: EXL3 routed experts, the trimmed lm_head and
 head-row metadata

The EXL3 build the pilot serves (card 40, 13.51 GiB): every layer that
stores a trellis per expert loads as mul1 3.0-bit EXL3 through the
grouped kernels - trellis bytes as stored, per-expert pointer tables,
stacked fp16 input/output scales, fp32 silu(gate)*up - and the routed
MoE launches gate/up then down through the shared grouped plan, leaving
fp32 sums for the combine, exactly as the FP8 and NVFP4 layers do.

A trimmed lm_head (drama_head_rows naming exactly the sampler's
candidate ids) uploads its rows as stored instead of gathering them from
the full vocabulary; anything else the metadata names is refused. The
expert map check now demands an EXL3 layer's trellis/suh/svh/mul1 set
complete, one of a kind per layer.
